Title
Call Center Queue Simulation

Aim
Simulate a call center using a queue. Implement addCall(customerID, callTime), answerCall(), viewQueue() and isQueueEmpty().

Parameters
Input: customer ID and call time. Output: queued calls and answered call. Add/answer/check-empty: O(1); viewing: O(n). Space: O(n).

Procedure
1. Create a FIFO queue.
2. Add customer ID and call time at the rear.
3. Answer and remove the first call.
4. Display all waiting calls.
5. Check whether the queue is empty.

Program

from collections import deque

q = deque()

def addCall(customerID, callTime):
    q.append((customerID, callTime))

def answerCall():
    if q:
        print("Answered:", q.popleft())
    else:
        print("No calls waiting.")

def viewQueue():
    print("Waiting calls:", list(q))

def isQueueEmpty():
    return len(q) == 0

addCall(101, 5)
addCall(102, 3)
addCall(103, 7)

viewQueue()
answerCall()
print("Queue empty:", isQueueEmpty())
viewQueue()
